entries.en:
What the robot has in its hands now: a list of products, one element per item, in the order it took them. Empty hands, an empty list. How many in all: `size()`, the first item: `get(0)`, whether there's such a product: `contains(p)`.

The list is a copy: changing it changes nothing in its hands. Goods are taken and put down by the robot's commands only.

```
// for example, [TOMATO, TOMATO] in its hands
List<Product> hands = robot.getCarried();
if (!hands.isEmpty()) {
    robot.putInBag(hands.get(0));           // what it took first
}
for (Product p : robot.getCarried()) {
    print("Carrying: " + p.getName());
}
```

This list has every method of any list, the same as the robot's own list `robot.getList()`. Press a plate and it opens. Their examples are on the robot's list; with the list from the hands it's all the same, only `add`, `set`, `remove` and `clear` change the copy, not the hands.

entries.ko:
로봇이 현재 손에 들고 있는 상품 목록입니다. 집어 든 순서대로 상품 하나당 요소 하나가 들어갑니다. 빈손이면 빈 목록입니다. 전체 개수는 `size()`, 첫 상품은 `get(0)`, 특정 상품의 포함 여부는 `contains(p)`로 확인합니다.

이 목록은 복사본입니다. 내용을 바꿔도 손에 든 상품은 바뀌지 않습니다. 실제로 상품을 집거나 내려놓는 것은 로봇 명령으로만 가능합니다.

```
                // for example, [TOMATO, TOMATO] in its hands
                List<Product> hands = robot.getCarried();
                if (!hands.isEmpty()) {
                    robot.putInBag(hands.get(0));           // what it took first
                }
                for (Product p : robot.getCarried()) {
